  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{9}$ by $2$, we repeat the fraction model $2$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/ae3caa583ee9745eb8bb79d6a00bb16373370b15bc272814100d6f10d6b4ad26.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $1\\times 2=2$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n2\\times \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$",
